        "original_id": "cc075e5d-f7fc-5eb4-81e5-430ba15a3726",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Lewis, Charlie Preedy\n- Organizations: Arsenal F.C., Cardiff City\n- Places: Highbury, London, England, Wales\n- Roles: Football goalkeeper\n- Events: 1927 FA Cup Final\n- Topics: Welsh football, Arsenal goalkeeping\n\nFacts:\n- Dan Lewis was born on 11 December 1902 and was a Welsh football goalkeeper.\n- Dan Lewis is most notable for playing for Arsenal.\n- In the 1927 FA Cup Final, Dan Lewis kept goal for Arsenal, and a mistake by him contributed to Cardiff City winning the cup.\n- Arsenal Football Club is a professional football club based in Highbury, London, England.\n- Arsenal Football Club plays in the Premier League, the top flight of English football.\n- Charlie Preedy was initially not Arsenal's first-team goalkeeper and mainly played as understudy to Dan Lewis, Arsenal's regular keeper.\n- Dan Lewis died in 1965.",
